            <ArticleTitle>[Unilateral isthmic lysis in x-ray computed tomography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>767-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Condensing pediculolaminar hypertrophy of mechanical origin is known as &quot;Dahu's sign&quot;. Dahu's sign corresponds to hypertrophy of the vertebral hemi-arch found by CT scan and leads to suspicion of controlateral lysis of the isthmus. It is the CT scan equivalent of vertebral &quot;anisocorism&quot; by conventional radiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
